<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23538" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾰτ-έομαι</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			18.264
		</span></i>, etc., irreg. inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δατέασθαι</span> (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έεσθαι</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				767
			</span></i>: fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάσομαι </span>(
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατα-ʼ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.354
				</span></i>
			 (tm.): aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδασάμην, δασσάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.208
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.368
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				Ion.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δασάσκετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.333
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δια-,</span> tm.): pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέδασμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diog.Apoll.
					3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				2.57
			</span></i> in pass. sense (v. infr. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>): aor.
			inf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δασθῆναι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>:—<i>divide among themselves,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτε κεν δατεώμεθα ληΐδ᾽ Ἀχαιοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.138
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μὲν εὖ δάσσαϝτο μετὰ σφίσιν υἷες
					Ἀχαιῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.368
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδιχα πάντα δάσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.511
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.335
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθόνα δατέοντο Ζεύς τε καὶ ἀθάνατοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					7.55
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μένος Ἄρηος δατέονται</span>
			<i>they share,</i> i.e. <i>are alike filled with,</i> the fury
			of Ares, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.264
			</span></i>: freq. of banqueters, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέα πολλὰ δατεῦντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.112
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοίρας δασσάμενοι δαίνυντ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.66
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέστην Ἕκτορα . . δώσελν κυσὶν
				ὠμὰ δάσασθαι</span>
			<i>tear</i> in pieces, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.21
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.87
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				450
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ἡμίονοι] χθόνα ποσσὶ δατεῦντο</span>
			<i>measured</i> the ground with their feet, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.121
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>cut in two,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν μὲν . . ἵπποι ἐπισσώτροις
					δατέοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.394
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in act.
			sense, simply, <i>divide,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρεῖς μοίρας δασάμενοι τὸν πεζόν</span>”
				<i>having divided into. .,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.121
				</span></i>
			; <i>divide</i> or <i>give</i> to others, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν θεῶν τᾡ ταχίστῳ . . τῶν θνητῶν
					τὸ τάχιστον δατέονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.216
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς παισὶ τὰ χρήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					279
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεῖον, πλέον δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					4.2.43
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Oec.</u>
				7.24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐπιβάλλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corn.
					<u>ND</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			: pf. in pass. sense, <i>to be divided,
				distributed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.125
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.189
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.84
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diog.Apoll.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				1329
			</span></i>.— 
				Ep.
			 and 
				Ion.
			, also Cret., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Leg.Gort.</u>
				4.28
			</span></i>, al., and <i><span class="en">Arc.,
					<u>IG</u>5(2).262</span></i>
			(Mantinea, <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>); rare in Trag., never in correct 
				Att.
			 Prose, exc. <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				7S.
			</span></i> (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίω</span> (B).)</div>
